Voice Mode keyboard dictionaries

The files in glide-dicts-v1/, bigram-dicts-v1/, trigram-dicts-v1/ and language-packs-v1/ are
unchanged copies of the release files of the same names published by DevEmperor in Dictate Keyboard
(https://github.com/DevEmperor/DictateKeyboard), licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE).
Copied on 2026-10-29; every file matched the size and SHA-256 that Dictate's app checks.

The files in ios-dicts-v1/ are the same word lists converted to the iPhone keyboard's file format.

whisper-models-v1/smart-turn-v3.2-cpu.onnx is an unchanged copy of the file of the same name in Dictate
Keyboard's whisper-models-v1 release (copied 2026-10-29, size and SHA-256 matched): Smart Turn v3,
© Pipecat AI, BSD-2-Clause (https://github.com/pipecat-ai/smart-turn), combined by Dictate with a
Whisper feature graph (Whisper © OpenAI, MIT).

The words themselves come from public data sets with their own terms, listed in attribution/:
  - OPUS OpenSubtitles frequency lists (J. Tiedemann, LREC 2012)
  - Leipzig Corpora Collection, CC BY (Universität Leipzig / Sächsische Akademie der Wissenschaften / InfAI)
  - Hunspell dictionaries, used at build time only to fix capitals and filter noise
  - CC-CEDICT, CC BY-SA 4.0 (the Chinese pinyin table, which carries the same licence)
